item.text:
Completed Chapter 7B research only. No scoring was performed.

The workspace was read-only and no filesystem-access tool was available, so `research-ledger-manifest.json` could not be read or updated. The ten `SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON` records below are the deterministic additive manifest payload for the parent ledger; existing entries must be retained unchanged.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PF diz que Bolsonaro não cometeu crime em inquérito sobre possível interferência na corporação","publisher":"Reuters via UOL","publication_date":"2022-03-30","url":"https://noticias.uol.com.br/ultimas-noticias/reuters/2022/03/30/pf-diz-que-bolsonaro-nao-cometeu-crime-em-inquerito-sobre-possivel-interferencia-na-corporacao.htm","claim":"The Federal Police concluded that Bolsonaro committed no crime in the inquiry into whether he directly interfered in the force's command, while Reuters noted that other investigations remained pending.","locator":"lines 503-511 and 528","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-001","canonical_fact_key":"https://noticias.uol.com.br/ultimas-noticias/reuters/2022/03/30/pf-diz-que-bolsonaro-nao-cometeu-crime-em-inquerito-sobre-possivel-interferencia-na-corporacao.htm|lines 503-511 and 528|Federal Police no-crime conclusion in interference inquiry","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.6","7B.7"],"source_type":"wire-service report of official investigation result","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters report identifying the Federal Police's formal conclusion; the underlying STF page was temporarily inaccessible.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Investigation concluded during the 2022 target period, although the alleged conduct began earlier.","ruler_attribution":"Direct inquiry into Bolsonaro's conduct; the finding is limiting evidence against personal obstruction attribution.","contrary_evidence":["Other STF and TSE inquiries remained pending and this conclusion did not resolve them."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Brazil: Freedom on the Net 2022 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/brazil/freedom-net/2022","claim":"Freedom House reported that election-related disinformation was largely amplified by Bolsonaro and allies, while also finding that news and human-rights organizations did not report technical attacks during the coverage period.","locator":"lines 85, 94-96 and 430-433","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-002","canonical_fact_key":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/brazil/freedom-net/2022|lines 85,94-96,430-433|Bolsonaro-allied disinformation amid continuing online reporting space","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.6","7B.10"],"source_type":"civil-society country monitoring report","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Established comparative monitor with cited examples, but some findings aggregate allies and broader conditions rather than Bolsonaro alone.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the run-up to the October 2022 election.","ruler_attribution":"Attributes amplification to Bolsonaro and allies; retaliation against journalists cannot uniformly be personalized to him.","contrary_evidence":["No technical attacks on news or human-rights organizations were reported in the coverage period.","Brazil retained vibrant online debate and reporting channels."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.6","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Referendadas liminares em ações sobre abusos de poder nas comemorações do Bicentenário da Independência","publisher":"Tribunal Superior Eleitoral","publication_date":"2022-09-13","url":"https://www.tse.jus.br/comunicacao/noticias/2022/Setembro/referendadas-liminares-em-acoes-sobre-abusos-de-poder-nas-comemoracoes-do-bicentenario-da-independencia","claim":"The TSE unanimously barred Bolsonaro and his running mate from using images from official Independence Day events in electoral propaganda and ordered removal of TV Brasil material, while the underlying abuse allegations remained under investigation.","locator":"lines 175-198, especially 184-187 and 197-198","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-003","canonical_fact_key":"https://www.tse.jus.br/comunicacao/noticias/2022/Setembro/referendadas-liminares-em-acoes-sobre-abusos-de-poder-nas-comemoracoes-do-bicentenario-da-independencia|lines 184-198|TSE restrictions on campaign use of official Independence Day imagery","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.3","7B.7","7B.9","7B.10"],"source_type":"official electoral-court record","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous official description of a unanimous interim ruling, with the preventive rather than final nature stated.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Official and campaign conduct occurred in September 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Bolsonaro personally appeared as president and reelection candidate; broader event financing involved multiple state and campaign actors.","contrary_evidence":["The ruling was an interim preventive measure, not yet a final merits finding in the cited record.","Some factual assertions about costs and intent were allegations by complainants."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.7","7B.9","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Com pacote de R$273 bi, uso da máquina impulsiona Bolsonaro na eleição e não tem punição à vista","publisher":"Reuters via UOL","publication_date":"2022-10-21","url":"https://noticias.uol.com.br/ultimas-noticias/reuters/2022/10/21/com-pacote-de-r273-bi-uso-da-maquina-impulsiona-bolsonaro-na-eleicao-e-nao-tem-punicao-a-vista.htm","claim":"Reuters calculated R$273 billion in implemented measures and commitments with 2022-2023 effects announced around the election, while distinguishing constitutionally authorized benefit expansion from measures that experts considered potentially punishable campaign-oriented use of policy.","locator":"lines 501-515 and 534-537","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-004","canonical_fact_key":"https://noticias.uol.com.br/ultimas-noticias/reuters/2022/10/21/com-pacote-de-r273-bi-uso-da-maquina-impulsiona-bolsonaro-na-eleicao-e-nao-tem-punicao-a-vista.htm|lines 508-515|Election-period policy package and disputed personal electoral advantage","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.3","7B.8","7B.9"],"source_type":"wire-service investigative analysis","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting with a disclosed aggregate calculation and named expert analysis; electoral motive and causal benefit were not adjudicated in the article.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Measures and announcements occurred during the 2022 reelection campaign.","ruler_attribution":"Bolsonaro announced or promoted the measures, but Congress authorized major components and programs also served legitimate social-policy purposes.","contrary_evidence":["The Auxílio Brasil increase was constitutionally authorized by Congress.","Correlation between spending and votes does not itself prove personal intent or causation.","The benefits delivered material assistance to eligible households."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.8","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Auditoria no Auxílio Brasil constata desvio do público-alvo do programa","publisher":"Tribunal de Contas da União","publication_date":"2022-12-15","url":"https://portal.tcu.gov.br/imprensa/noticias/auditoria-no-auxilio-brasil-constata-desvio-do-publico-alvo-do-programa","claim":"A TCU audit found program-design incentives for false household-composition declarations, estimated possible improper payments exceeding R$2 billion monthly, and found Auxílio Brasil less cost-effective at reducing the poverty gap than Bolsa Família.","locator":"lines 6-27; decision identified at lines 31-35 as Acórdão 2725/2022, TC 007.871/2022-8","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-005","canonical_fact_key":"https://portal.tcu.gov.br/imprensa/noticias/auditoria-no-auxilio-brasil-constata-desvio-do-publico-alvo-do-programa|lines 15-26|TCU audit of Auxílio Brasil targeting and cost-effectiveness","disposition":"context","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.3","7B.8","7B.9"],"source_type":"official audit summary","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official TCU audit summary with case number, decision, quantified estimates, and recommendations.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Audit and underlying program operation fall within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Bolsonaro had executive authority over federal program design and administration, but Congress, the responsible ministry, CadÚnico administration, and beneficiary declarations divide attribution.","contrary_evidence":["The audit did not find that Bolsonaro personally received funds or personally directed improper enrollments.","TCU recommendations show that independent auditing remained operational."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.8","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"TSE declara inelegibilidade do ex-presidente Jair Bolsonaro","publisher":"Tribunal Superior Eleitoral","publication_date":"2023-06-30","url":"https://www.tse.jus.br/comunicacao/radio/2023/Junho/tse-declara-inelegibilidade-do-ex-presidente-jair-bolsonaro","claim":"By five votes to two, the TSE found abuse of political power and misuse of media in Bolsonaro's July 2022 meeting with foreign ambassadors, where official presidential resources were used to challenge the electoral system.","locator":"headline, deck, and publication block; companion vote summary at https://www.tse.jus.br/comunicacao/noticias/2023/Junho/com-o-placar-de-3x1-pela-inelegibilidade-de-bolsonaro-tse-suspende-julgamento, paragraphs beginning 'O Plenário' and 'Houve desvio de finalidade'","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-006","canonical_fact_key":"https://www.tse.jus.br/comunicacao/radio/2023/Junho/tse-declara-inelegibilidade-do-ex-presidente-jair-bolsonaro|headline and deck|Final TSE finding on Bolsonaro's 2022 ambassadors meeting","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.1","7B.3","7B.7","7B.10"],"source_type":"official final electoral-court disposition","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official court report of a completed merits vote; the 5-2 split supplies an explicit contrary judicial view.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Decision was issued in 2023, but adjudicated Bolsonaro's personal conduct in July 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct: Bolsonaro convened and spoke at the meeting using the presidency's diplomatic and communications apparatus.","contrary_evidence":["Two judges dissented.","Braga Netto was excluded because his responsibility was not demonstrated, limiting network attribution."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.3","7B.7","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Partidos questionam graça concedida por Bolsonaro ao deputado Daniel Silveira","publisher":"Supremo Tribunal Federal","publication_date":"2022-04-22","url":"https://noticias.stf.jus.br/postsnoticias/partidos-questionam-graca-concedida-por-bolsonaro-ao-deputado-daniel-silveira/","claim":"Bolsonaro issued an individual pardon to political ally Daniel Silveira one day after the STF sentenced Silveira for threats to democratic rule and coercion in judicial proceedings; the STF later invalidated the decree by majority.","locator":"paragraphs 1-2; final disposition recorded in ADPF 964 process page dated 10/05/2023 at https://portal.stf.jus.br/processos/detalhe.asp?incidente=6389572","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-007","canonical_fact_key":"https://noticias.stf.jus.br/postsnoticias/partidos-questionam-graca-concedida-por-bolsonaro-ao-deputado-daniel-silveira/|paragraphs 1-2|Bolsonaro's 2022 individual pardon of Daniel Silveira","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.7","7B.9","7B.10"],"source_type":"official court news and docket record","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"The decree, conviction timing, legal challenge, and later majority invalidation are documented by the STF.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pardon was issued on 21 April 2022; final judicial review occurred in 2023.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential act personally signed by Bolsonaro.","contrary_evidence":["The constitutional pardon power existed and two justices dissented from the later invalidation.","The invalidation postdates the target period."],"lenses":["7B.7","7B.9","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Como a desinformação sobre urnas abasteceu a artilharia de Bolsonaro contra o sistema eleitoral","publisher":"Aos Fatos","publication_date":"2022-06-06","url":"https://www.aosfatos.org/noticias/desinformacao-urnas-abasteceu-artilharia-bolsonaro-contra-sistema-eleitoral/","claim":"Aos Fatos identified at least 84 Bolsonaro allegations since 2018 concerning election fraud or voting-system weakness and reported that none had been substantiated, documenting repeated claims rather than a single incident.","locator":"opening four paragraphs, especially paragraph beginning 'Em setembro de 2018'","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-008","canonical_fact_key":"https://www.aosfatos.org/noticias/desinformacao-urnas-abasteceu-artilharia-bolsonaro-contra-sistema-eleitoral/|opening four paragraphs|At least 84 unsupported Bolsonaro election-system allegations","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"],"source_type":"local-language fact-checking investigation","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Named fact-checking organization describes a systematic statement-level review, but the count spans 2018-2022 and should not be treated as 84 separate 2022 events.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Published during 2022 and includes a longitudinal pattern continuing into the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Direct public statements by Bolsonaro; supporter-generated misinformation was separately distinguished.","contrary_evidence":["The total spans several years, so it is pattern evidence rather than a 2022-only incident count.","Robust TSE audits and open fact-checking provided public correction mechanisms."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Relatório sobre Violações à Liberdade de Expressão 2022","publisher":"Associação Brasileira de Emissoras de Rádio e Televisão (ABERT)","publication_date":"2023-05","url":"https://www.abert.org.br/link/2023/abert_relatorio_anual_2022_com_casos_v05.pdf","claim":"ABERT reported that Bolsonaro had repeatedly offended, delegitimized, or disqualified journalists and disclosed reporters' personal information, and noted a court award of R$100,000 to the journalists' professional category.","locator":"PDF p. 35, section 'Decisões judiciais'","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-009","canonical_fact_key":"https://www.abert.org.br/link/2023/abert_relatorio_anual_2022_com_casos_v05.pdf|p.35, Decisões judiciais|Repeated Bolsonaro attacks on journalists and judicial response","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"],"source_type":"press-association annual monitoring report","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Sector association supplies a specific judicial outcome and documented pattern; broader attack totals include allies and cannot all be attributed to Bolsonaro.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The report covers 2022, although the described pattern spans Bolsonaro's full presidency.","ruler_attribution":"The specified conduct and damages judgment concern Bolsonaro directly; other violence and online attacks in the report have mixed perpetrators.","contrary_evidence":["Courts remained available and issued both press-favorable and press-adverse decisions.","The report recorded 11 favorable and nine unfavorable press-related judicial decisions, showing a mixed legal environment rather than total suppression."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bolsonaro under fire over claims family paid for 51 properties in cash","publisher":"The Guardian","publication_date":"2022-08-30","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/30/jair-bolsonaro-brazil-property-payments-cash-allegations","claim":"Reporting based on a seven-month UOL investigation alleged that members of Bolsonaro's extended family used cash to purchase 51 of 107 properties between 1990 and 2022, prompting scrutiny but not establishing that Jair Bolsonaro personally profited from office or that the funds were illicit.","locator":"opening six paragraphs","provisional_id":"WEB-7B-010","canonical_fact_key":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/30/jair-bolsonaro-brazil-property-payments-cash-allegations|opening six paragraphs|Allegations concerning extended Bolsonaro-family cash property purchases","disposition":"context","chapter_ids":["7B"],"methodology_ids":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.6"],"source_type":"international press report based on local investigative reporting","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"The purchases and investigative methodology were reported contemporaneously, but sources of funds, illegality, office nexus, and Jair Bolsonaro's personal benefit were not established.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Published in 2022, but the transactions span 1990-2022 and many predate Bolsonaro's presidency.","ruler_attribution":"Weak and heterogeneous: the reported purchasers include Bolsonaro, former spouses, children, siblings, and an in-law.","contrary_evidence":["Cash purchase was legal in Brazil.","The report did not prove illicit funding, a state-decision nexus, or personal profit from the presidency.","Bolsonaro responded that each relative had an independent life and finances."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.6"]}

Two prior records were reopened and verified, but are not newly discovered documents:

- `E040`: The TSE’s 27 September ruling is verified at lines 168-189. It prohibited campaign livestreams from presidential palaces using publicly funded services and found indications that exclusive state resources produced campaign material. [TSE ruling](https://www.tse.jus.br/comunicacao/noticias/2022/Setembro/plenario-decide-que-bolsonaro-nao-pode-transmitir-lives-eleitorais-em-espacos-exclusivos-do-presidente-da-republica/)
- `E045`: Bolsonaro’s denial of the “15 million hungry” figure and the comparison with FAO estimates are verified at lines 508-521. The distinction between severe food insecurity and the colloquial meaning of hunger should remain explicit. [Reuters/UOL report](https://economia.uol.com.br/noticias/reuters/2022/08/26/bolsonaro-rejeita-discurso-de-que-ha-15-milhoes-passando-fome-no-brasil-e-exalta-auxilio-brasil.htm)

Research-wave accounting:

- Documents discovered: 44
- Promising underlying documents opened or directly inspected: 17
- Accepted: 12 source-claim units—10 new and 2 reused
- Rejected after review: 23
- Access-blocked or technically incomplete: 4
- Remaining discovery leads not retained: 5
- Distinct accepted source organizations: 8
- Source types: official electoral rulings, official court/docket records, official audit, wire-service reporting, fact-checking investigation, comparative civil-society monitoring, press-association report, and investigative press reporting

Lens coverage:

- `7B.1`: Strong evidence of repeated unsupported election claims, the ambassadors meeting, and the food-insecurity denial.
- `7B.2`: Evidence of repetition/doubling down and treatment of journalists; no well-documented 2022 example of Bolsonaro voluntarily correcting a material false claim.
- `7B.3`: Stronger for mixing incumbency resources and reelection activity; weak for business, licensing, procurement, or foreign-policy conflicts.
- `7B.4`: Residual major gap. Family-property reporting is allegation/context only. No target-period adjudication establishes personal or close-family profit from office.
- `7B.5`: Residual major gap. Military and loyalist appointments are documented in the source landscape, but the wave found insufficient appointment-by-appointment evidence connecting 2022 selections to incompetence, self-dealing, or yes-man protection.
- `7B.6`: Mixed evidence: multiple investigations, audits, courts, media, and fact-checkers operated; secrecy and attacks created friction, but complete intolerance of investigation is not established.
- `7B.7`: Evidence includes use of state communications/resources, the Silveira pardon, and pressure on accountability institutions; the Federal Police no-crime finding is material contrary evidence.
- `7B.8`: Repeated election narratives and disputed campaign-period policy shifts are relevant, but systematic promise-keeping evidence remains limited.
- `7B.9`: Evidence supports favoritism/transactional-politics concerns in pardons and campaign-linked public-resource use. Procurement favoritism and personal enforcement favors remain unproven.
- `7B.10`: Strong pattern evidence concerning misinformation, institutional attacks, press treatment, and public/private-role boundaries, tempered by functioning judicial, audit, media, and electoral checks.

Another Chapter 7B-specific search wave would have only targeted value, chiefly for `7B.4` and `7B.5`: primary asset declarations, procurement records, appointment files, and final judicial records could materially improve those lenses. A broad repeat search is unlikely to add much because public-claim, election-resource, pardon, press-treatment, and audit evidence is already saturated and carries high duplicate-event risk.
